# Depends mirrors UNISIC_DEBIAN_RUNTIME_DEPENDS in CMakeLists.txt and must stay
# CHARACTER-IDENTICAL to it: the explicit entries cover runtime-loaded pieces
# ${shlibs:Depends} cannot see (QML modules, the Qt SVG image plugin, the
# pipewire daemon, the ffmpeg/curl/zip CLIs, portals, wl-clipboard, the
# tesseract language data). None of them is a Recommends - Unisic has no
# optional dependencies, and an install that cannot record, cannot upload over
# sftp, cannot build a diagnostics bundle and has an empty OCR language list is
# a broken install, not a degraded one. Only the portal BACKEND stays weak,
# because a session always has one and choosing for the user would pull in half
# a foreign desktop.
# Build-Depends mirror the debian:trixie CI job in .github/workflows/deb.yml
# and the Build-Depends line in unisic.dsc, and cover all 11 compile-time gates
# (each is REQUIRED in CMakeLists.txt now, so a missing one fails configure
# with the package name to install instead of silently dropping a feature).
Source: unisic
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Unisic maintainers <unisic@debondor.com>
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/unisic/unisic
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake, ninja-build, g++, pkg-config,
 extra-cmake-modules,
 qt6-base-dev, qt6-declarative-dev, qt6-svg-dev, qt6-tools-dev, qt6-l10n-tools,
 qt6-wayland-dev, qt6-base-private-dev, plasma-wayland-protocols,
 libpipewire-0.3-dev, libtesseract-dev, libleptonica-dev, libzxing-dev,
 liblayershellqtinterface-dev, libwayland-dev, libkf6guiaddons-dev,
 libx11-dev, libxext-dev, libxfixes-dev, libxcb1-dev,
 libinput-dev, libudev-dev

Package: unisic
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, curl, ffmpeg, libqt6svg6,
 pipewire, qml6-module-qtmultimedia, qml6-module-qtquick,
 qml6-module-qtquick-controls, qml6-module-qtquick-dialogs,
 qml6-module-qtquick-effects, qml6-module-qtquick-window, qt6-wayland,
 tesseract-ocr-eng, tesseract-ocr-osd, tesseract-ocr-pol, wl-clipboard,
 xdg-desktop-portal, zip
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-kde | xdg-desktop-portal-gnome |
 xdg-desktop-portal-wlr | xdg-desktop-portal-lxqt | xdg-desktop-portal-phosh |
 xdg-desktop-portal-gtk | xdg-desktop-portal-xapp
Description: Capture, annotate, record and share your screen on Linux Wayland
 Unisic covers the whole workflow after you press the hotkey: annotate on the
 selection overlay before the shot is taken, keep editing afterwards (blur,
 pixelate, numbered steps, crop, object cutout), record the same region as
 GIF/MP4/WebM, and push the result to the clipboard, disk or a custom upload
 destination. Built for Wayland on legitimate APIs (xdg-desktop-portal, KWin
 ScreenShot2, PipeWire, KGlobalAccel), with a fully silent native capture
 path on KDE Plasma. Zero telemetry.
